/* Verse Games: THE WHOLE COUNSEL · 2 Samuel chapters 16-20
   Verse text is filled/verified from the KJV by tools/fill-verses.js */
VG.registerBibleChapters("2samuel", [
{n:16, name:"Shimei's Curse", seal:{ref:"2 Samuel 16:12",verse:"It may be that the LORD will look on mine affliction, and that the LORD will requite me good for his cursing this day."}, facts:["Did you know Ziba arrived with two hundred loaves of bread, a hundred bunches of raisins, a hundred of summer fruits, and a bottle of wine, and was rewarded with Mephibosheth's whole estate on the word of a slander (2 Samuel 16:1, 16:4)?","Did you know Shimei cursed David as a 'bloody man' and a 'man of Belial' while throwing stones, and Abishai had to be stopped from taking his head on the spot (2 Samuel 16:7, 16:9)?","Did you know Ahithophel's counsel was so prized that it was regarded 'as if a man had enquired at the oracle of God,' whether he spoke to David or to Absalom (2 Samuel 16:23)?"], questions:[
{q:"Who met David with a couple of asses saddled and loaded with food?", options:["Ziba, the servant of Mephibosheth","Mephibosheth himself","Shimei the son of Gera","Abiathar the priest"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 16:1",verse:"And when David was a little past the top of the hill, behold, Ziba the servant of Mephibosheth met him, with a couple of asses saddled, and upon them two hundred loaves of bread, and an hundred bunches of raisins, and an hundred of summer fruits, and a bottle of wine.", insight:"Ziba came loaded with provision at David's lowest moment; bring your best to those who are fleeing, not only to those who are feasting."},
{q:"Besides two hundred loaves of bread, what did Ziba bring?", options:["An hundred bunches of raisins, an hundred of summer fruits, and a bottle of wine","Cakes of figs and clusters of grapes only","Roasted lamb and unleavened bread","Cheese of kine and parched corn"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 16:1",verse:"And when David was a little past the top of the hill, behold, Ziba the servant of Mephibosheth met him, with a couple of asses saddled, and upon them two hundred loaves of bread, and an hundred bunches of raisins, and an hundred of summer fruits, and a bottle of wine.", insight:"Bread for the young men, wine for the faint; thoughtful giving meets the need it sees."},
{q:"According to Ziba, what were the asses for?", options:["For the king's household to ride on","For carrying armor into battle","For the priests to ride to Jerusalem","For plowing the fields at Bahurim"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 16:2",verse:"And the king said unto Ziba, What meanest thou by these? And Ziba said, The asses be for the king’s household to ride on; and the bread and summer fruit for the young men to eat; and the wine, that such as be faint in the wilderness may drink.", insight:"Every gift had its purpose; Ziba had thought it through, which is why David trusted him too quickly."},
{q:"What did Ziba claim Mephibosheth had said in Jerusalem?", options:["Today shall the house of Israel restore me the kingdom of my father","David is finished and Absalom is king","Ziba has stolen all my goods","I will follow David into exile"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 16:3",verse:"And the king said, And where is thy master’s son? And Ziba said unto the king, Behold, he abideth at Jerusalem: for he said, Today shall the house of Israel restore me the kingdom of my father.", insight:"A slander spoken at the right moment can steal an inheritance; David believed it without asking."},
{q:"How did David reward Ziba's report?", options:["Behold, thine are all that pertained unto Mephibosheth","He made Ziba prince over Benjamin","He gave him only the asses and the food","He sent him back to Jerusalem"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 16:4",verse:"Then said the king to Ziba, Behold, thine are all that pertained unto Mephibosheth. And Ziba said, I humbly beseech thee that I may find grace in thy sight, my lord, O king.", insight:"David gave away another man's estate on one man's word; hasty judgments in hard times wound the innocent."},
{q:"Who came out from Bahurim cursing David?", options:["Shimei the son of Gera","Ziba the servant","Ahithophel the Gilonite","Sheba the son of Bichri"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 16:5",verse:"And when king David came to Bahurim, behold, thence came out a man of the family of the house of Saul, whose name was Shimei, the son of Gera: he came forth, and cursed still as he came.", insight:"Shimei belonged to the house of Saul; old grudges wait for weak moments to speak."},
{q:"What did Shimei do as he cursed?", options:["He cast stones at David and at all his servants","He drew his sword and challenged them","He set fire to their camp","He blocked the road with thorns"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 16:6",verse:"And he cast stones at David, and at all the servants of king David: and all the people and all the mighty men were on his right hand and on his left.", insight:"Stones and curses together; some men throw whatever their hands can find."},
{q:"What names did Shimei call David?", options:["Thou bloody man, and thou man of Belial","Thou thief and thou liar","Thou coward and thou traitor","Thou fool and thou stranger"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 16:7",verse:"And thus said Shimei when he cursed, Come out, come out, thou bloody man, and thou man of Belial:", insight:"'Bloody man' stung because David knew his own sins; a curse lands hardest where conscience is tender."},
{q:"What did Shimei say the LORD had done to David?", options:["Returned upon him all the blood of the house of Saul, and delivered the kingdom to Absalom","Cast him out of the covenant forever","Given his wives to another man","Struck him with leprosy"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 16:8",verse:"The LORD hath returned upon thee all the blood of the house of Saul, in whose stead thou hast reigned; and the LORD hath delivered the kingdom into the hand of Absalom thy son: and, behold, thou art taken in thy mischief, because thou art a bloody man.", insight:"Shimei preached judgment with his stones; even true words about justice turn cruel in a cursing mouth."},
{q:"What did Abishai ask permission to do?", options:["Go over and take off Shimei's head","Arrest Shimei and bind him","Answer Shimei curse for curse","Drive Shimei out of Bahurim"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 16:9",verse:"Then said Abishai the son of Zeruiah unto the king, Why should this dead dog curse my lord the king? let me go over, I pray thee, and take off his head.", insight:"Abishai's loyalty was fierce and fast; David's restraint was the harder courage."},
{q:"How did David answer Abishai?", options:["What have I to do with you, ye sons of Zeruiah? So let him curse","Take him now, but spare his house","Bind him until the battle is over","Pay no heed, the man is mad"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 16:10",verse:"And the king said, What have I to do with you, ye sons of Zeruiah? so let him curse, because the LORD hath said unto him, Curse David. Who shall then say, Wherefore hast thou done so?", insight:"David would not silence the curser; he left the matter between Shimei and God."},
{q:"Why did David let Shimei curse?", options:["Because the LORD had said unto him, Curse David","Because he feared Absalom's spies","Because Shimei was a prophet","Because the law forbade it"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 16:11",verse:"And David said to Abishai, and to all his servants, Behold, my son, which came forth of my bowels, seeketh my life: how much more now may this Benjamite do it? let him alone, and let him curse; for the LORD hath bidden him.", insight:"'Let him alone, and let him curse'; David heard God's hand even in a man's hatred."},
{q:"What hope did David express about the cursing?", options:["It may be that the LORD will requite me good for his cursing this day","The LORD would strike Shimei dead","Absalom would pardon them both","The people would rise and defend him"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 16:12",verse:"It may be that the LORD will look on mine affliction, and that the LORD will requite me good for his cursing this day.", insight:"David hoped affliction might turn to good; humility looks for mercy even in mockery."},
{q:"What did Shimei keep doing as he went along the hillside?", options:["Cursing, throwing stones, and casting dust","Singing songs of Saul's victories","Gathering men to join Absalom","Praying loudly for David's fall"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 16:13",verse:"And as David and his men went by the way, Shimei went along on the hill’s side over against him, and cursed as he went, and threw stones at him, and cast dust.", insight:"He walked parallel to the king, cursing the whole way; bitterness is a long and dusty road."},
{q:"What did David and his weary people do when they came to their rest?", options:["They refreshed themselves there","They built an altar and sacrificed","They numbered their fighting men","They sent messengers to Absalom"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 16:14",verse:"And the king, and all the people that were with him, came weary, and refreshed themselves there.", insight:"Weary and cursed, they rested; even a fleeing king must sit down and breathe."},
{q:"What did Hushai cry out when Absalom came to Jerusalem?", options:["God save the king, God save the king","Long live Absalom the king","Peace to the house of David","The LORD has delivered thee"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 16:16",verse:"And it came to pass, when Hushai the Archite, David’s friend, was come unto Absalom, that Hushai said unto Absalom, God save the king, God save the king.", insight:"Hushai played his dangerous part well; the cry that once honored David now shielded David's spy."},
{q:"How did Absalom question Hushai's loyalty?", options:["Is this thy kindness to thy friend? Why wentest thou not with thy friend?","Where is the ark of God?","Who sent thee to Jerusalem?","Art thou also a traitor?"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 16:17",verse:"And Absalom said to Hushai, Is this thy kindness to thy friend? why wentest thou not with thy friend?", insight:"Absalom suspected the very loyalty he was stealing; usurpers trust no one."},
{q:"What counsel did Ahithophel give Absalom?", options:["Go in unto thy father's concubines, which he left to keep the house","Kill Hushai before he betrays thee","Burn David's palace to the ground","Pursue David this very night"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 16:21",verse:"And Ahithophel said unto Absalom, Go in unto thy father’s concubines, which he hath left to keep the house; and all Israel shall hear that thou art abhorred of thy father: then shall the hands of all that are with thee be strong.", insight:"Ahithophel's counsel was cruel and public; he wanted the break with David to be beyond repair."},
{q:"Where did they spread a tent for Absalom?", options:["Upon the top of the house","In the king's dale","Before the gate of the city","In the court of the temple"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 16:22",verse:"So they spread Absalom a tent upon the top of the house; and Absalom went in unto his father’s concubines in the sight of all Israel.", insight:"On the rooftop, in sight of all Israel; sin loves a stage when it wants to prove a point."},
{q:"How was Ahithophel's counsel regarded in those days?", options:["As if a man had enquired at the oracle of God","As the babbling of a drunkard","As the cunning of a serpent","As the wisdom of Egypt"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 16:23",verse:"And the counsel of Ahithophel, which he counselled in those days, was as if a man had enquired at the oracle of God: so was all the counsel of Ahithophel both with David and with Absalom.", insight:"Men treated his words as oracles; trusted counsel can still counsel evil."}
]},
{n:17, name:"The Counsel Defeated", seal:{ref:"2 Samuel 17:14",verse:"And Absalom and all the men of Israel said, The counsel of Hushai the Archite is better than the counsel of Ahithophel. For the LORD had appointed to defeat the good counsel of Ahithophel, to the intent that the LORD might bring evil upon Absalom."}, facts:["Did you know Ahithophel's plan needed only twelve thousand men and a single night to kill David while he was weary and weak handed, and it would likely have worked had Hushai not spoken (2 Samuel 17:1-2)?","Did you know Jonathan and Ahimaaz were hidden down a well at Bahurim while a woman spread ground corn over the well's mouth to fool Absalom's servants (2 Samuel 17:18-19)?","Did you know three men, Shobi, Machir, and Barzillai, brought beds, wheat, barley, honey, butter, sheep, and cheese to feed David's hungry, weary, and thirsty people at Mahanaim (2 Samuel 17:27-29)?"], questions:[
{q:"How many men did Ahithophel ask to choose for the pursuit?", options:["Twelve thousand","Three thousand","Thirty thousand","A thousand"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 17:1",verse:"Moreover Ahithophel said unto Absalom, Let me now choose out twelve thousand men, and I will arise and pursue after David this night:", insight:"Twelve thousand for one weary man; evil overestimates what it needs and underestimates God."},
{q:"When did Ahithophel want to pursue David?", options:["This night","At the new moon","After the sabbath","When the rains ended"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 17:1",verse:"Moreover Ahithophel said unto Absalom, Let me now choose out twelve thousand men, and I will arise and pursue after David this night:", insight:"'This night'; haste is the friend of wicked counsel."},
{q:"Whom did Ahithophel plan to strike?", options:["The king only","David and his mighty men","The priests Zadok and Abiathar","All who fled Jerusalem"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 17:2",verse:"And I will come upon him while he is weary and weak handed, and will make him afraid: and all the people that are with him shall flee; and I will smite the king only:", insight:"'I will smite the king only'; remove the shepherd and the sheep scatter, or so he thought."},
{q:"How did Ahithophel describe David's state?", options:["Weary and weak handed","Proud and unguarded","Old and half blind","Angry and reckless"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 17:2",verse:"And I will come upon him while he is weary and weak handed, and will make him afraid: and all the people that are with him shall flee; and I will smite the king only:", insight:"He counted on David's weariness; God counts His people's weakness as the place He shows His strength."},
{q:"What did Ahithophel promise about David's people?", options:["The man thou seekest is as if all returned, so all the people shall be in peace","They would all be put to the sword","They would be sold into Egypt","They would crown Absalom gladly"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 17:3",verse:"And I will bring back all the people unto thee: the man whom thou seekest is as if all returned: so all the people shall be in peace.", insight:"One death, and all in peace; tidy plans rarely survive contact with God."},
{q:"How was Ahithophel's counsel received?", options:["The saying pleased Absalom well, and all the elders of Israel","It was rejected as too cruel","They laughed it to scorn","They asked for a second opinion at once"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 17:4",verse:"And the saying pleased Absalom well, and all the elders of Israel.", insight:"It pleased them well; popular counsel is not always godly counsel."},
{q:"Whom did Absalom call to hear also?", options:["Hushai the Archite","Zadok the priest","Nathan the prophet","Joab the captain"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 17:5",verse:"Then said Absalom, Call now Hushai the Archite also, and let us hear likewise what he saith.", insight:"One more voice, at the very moment it mattered; God slipped Hushai into the room."},
{q:"What did Hushai say of Ahithophel's counsel?", options:["It is not good at this time","It is the wisdom of God","It is too gentle by half","It should wait till morning"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 17:7",verse:"And Hushai said unto Absalom, The counsel that Ahithophel hath given is not good at this time.", insight:"'Not good at this time'; sometimes the bravest word is a quiet no."},
{q:"To what did Hushai liken David's chafed mighty men?", options:["A bear robbed of her whelps in the field","A lioness guarding her den","A serpent coiled to strike","An eagle guarding its nest"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 17:8",verse:"For, said Hushai, thou knowest thy father and his men, that they be mighty men, and they be chafed in their minds, as a bear robbed of her whelps in the field: and thy father is a man of war, and will not lodge with the people.", insight:"A bear robbed of her whelps; Hushai painted David's men as dangerous to wake."},
{q:"What did Hushai counsel instead?", options:["Gather all Israel from Dan to Beersheba, and let Absalom go to battle in his own person","Sue for peace with David at once","Fortify Jerusalem and wait","Send gifts to win David back"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 17:11",verse:"Therefore I counsel that all Israel be generally gathered unto thee, from Dan even to Beer-sheba, as the sand that is by the sea for multitude; and that thou go to battle in thine own person.", insight:"Flattery dressed as strategy; Hushai fed Absalom's pride to buy David time."},
{q:"How did Hushai say they would fall upon David?", options:["As the dew falleth on the ground","As fire devours stubble","As the night covers the hills","As the flood sweeps the valley"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 17:12",verse:"So shall we come upon him in some place where he shall be found, and we will light upon him as the dew falleth on the ground: and of him and of all the men that are with him there shall not be left so much as one.", insight:"Like dew, soft and everywhere; Hushai's poetry hid a delay."},
{q:"What would they do if David hid in a city?", options:["Bring ropes and draw it into the river till not one stone remained","Starve it out for seven years","Burn its gates with fire","Leave it and march on"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 17:13",verse:"Moreover, if he be gotten into a city, then shall all Israel bring ropes to that city, and we will draw it into the river, until there be not one small stone found there.", insight:"Ropes to drag a city into the river; big talk bought the hours David needed."},
{q:"Whose counsel did Absalom and all Israel prefer?", options:["The counsel of Hushai the Archite","The counsel of Ahithophel","The counsel of the elders","No counsel at all"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 17:14",verse:"And Absalom and all the men of Israel said, The counsel of Hushai the Archite is better than the counsel of Ahithophel. For the LORD had appointed to defeat the good counsel of Ahithophel, to the intent that the LORD might bring evil upon Absalom.", insight:"They chose the flattering plan; pride picks the counsel that crowns it."},
{q:"Why was Ahithophel's good counsel defeated?", options:["The LORD had appointed to defeat it, to bring evil upon Absalom","Hushai bribed the elders","The men refused to march at night","David's spies stole the plan"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 17:14",verse:"And Absalom and all the men of Israel said, The counsel of Hushai the Archite is better than the counsel of Ahithophel. For the LORD had appointed to defeat the good counsel of Ahithophel, to the intent that the LORD might bring evil upon Absalom.", insight:"Behind the debate stood the LORD, appointing; no counsel stands when God has decided."},
{q:"What warning did Hushai send to David that night?", options:["Lodge not this night in the plains of the wilderness, but speedily pass over","Hide in the caves of Engedi","Return to Jerusalem at dawn","Flee to the Philistines"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 17:16",verse:"Now therefore send quickly, and tell David, saying, Lodge not this night in the plains of the wilderness, but speedily pass over; lest the king be swallowed up, and all the people that are with him.", insight:"'Speedily pass over'; God's warnings come with urgency, and David moved."},
{q:"Where were Jonathan and Ahimaaz hidden at Bahurim?", options:["Down in a well in a man's court","In a cave behind the house","Under sheaves in the barn","In the cistern of the city"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 17:18",verse:"Nevertheless a lad saw them, and told Absalom: but they went both of them away quickly, and came to a man’s house in Bahurim, which had a well in his court; whither they went down.", insight:"A well became a hiding place; God uses ordinary household things to save His messengers."},
{q:"How did the woman conceal the well's mouth?", options:["She spread a covering and ground corn over it","She piled stones upon it","She covered it with branches","She sat upon it herself"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 17:19",verse:"And the woman took and spread a covering over the well’s mouth, and spread ground corn thereon; and the thing was not known.", insight:"Ground corn over a well; quick wits in a brave woman saved two lives."},
{q:"By morning light, how many of David's people had failed to cross Jordan?", options:["Not one","A dozen","Half the little ones","The rear guard"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 17:22",verse:"Then David arose, and all the people that were with him, and they passed over Jordan: by the morning light there lacked not one of them that was not gone over Jordan.", insight:"Not one lacked; when God says pass over, the whole company gets across."},
{q:"What did Ahithophel do when his counsel was rejected?", options:["He put his household in order, hanged himself, and died","He fled to the Philistines","He begged Absalom's pardon","He joined David in exile"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 17:23",verse:"And when Ahithophel saw that his counsel was not followed, he saddled his ass, and arose, and gat him home to his house, to his city, and put his household in order, and hanged himself, and died, and was buried in the sepulchre of his father.", insight:"Rejected counsel became a noose; pride would rather die than be overruled."},
{q:"Whom did Absalom make captain of the host instead of Joab?", options:["Amasa","Abishai","Ittai the Gittite","Benaiah"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 17:25",verse:"And Absalom made Amasa captain of the host instead of Joab: which Amasa was a man’s son, whose name was Ithra an Israelite, that went in to Abigail the daughter of Nahash, sister to Zeruiah Joab’s mother.", insight:"Amasa took Joab's place; the appointment would cost him his life within the year."}
]},
{n:18, name:"Absalom's Fall", seal:{ref:"2 Samuel 18:33",verse:"And the king was much moved, and went up to the chamber over the gate, and wept: and as he went, thus he said, O my son Absalom, my son, my son Absalom! would God I had died for thee, O Absalom, my son, my son!"}, facts:["Did you know the wood of Ephraim killed more of Absalom's men that day than the sword did, as the battle scattered over the face of all the country (2 Samuel 18:8)?","Did you know Absalom was left hanging between heaven and earth when his head caught in the thick boughs of a great oak and his mule walked on without him (2 Samuel 18:9)?","Did you know Absalom set up a pillar in the king's dale in his lifetime because, as he said, 'I have no son to keep my name in remembrance,' and it is called Absalom's place to this day (2 Samuel 18:18)?"], questions:[
{q:"How did David divide his army?", options:["A third under Joab, a third under Abishai, and a third under Ittai the Gittite","Half under Joab and half under Abishai","Into twelve tribes as in the wilderness","He kept them all together"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 18:2",verse:"And David sent forth a third part of the people under the hand of Joab, and a third part under the hand of Abishai the son of Zeruiah, Joab’s brother, and a third part under the hand of Ittai the Gittite. And the king said unto the people, I will surely go forth with you myself also.", insight:"Three captains, three thirds; David ordered his house even with his heart breaking."},
{q:"Why did the people refuse to let David go to battle?", options:["Thou art worth ten thousand of us","He was too old to fight","The law forbade the king to fight","Absalom would target him first"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 18:3",verse:"But the people answered, Thou shalt not go forth: for if we flee away, they will not care for us; neither if half of us die, will they care for us: but now thou art worth ten thousand of us: therefore now it is better that thou succour us out of the city.", insight:"'Thou art worth ten thousand of us'; they loved the king they would not risk."},
{q:"What charge did David give his captains concerning Absalom?", options:["Deal gently for my sake with the young man, even with Absalom","Spare no rebel, young or old","Take Absalom alive at all costs","Let Absalom escape to Geshur"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 18:5",verse:"And the king commanded Joab and Abishai and Ittai, saying, Deal gently for my sake with the young man, even with Absalom. And all the people heard when the king gave all the captains charge concerning Absalom.", insight:"'Deal gently for my sake'; a father's heart spoke louder than a king's justice."},
{q:"Where was the battle fought?", options:["In the wood of Ephraim","In the valley of Elah","At the pool of Gibeon","On the plains of Jericho"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 18:6",verse:"So the people went out into the field against Israel: and the battle was in the wood of Ephraim;", insight:"The wood of Ephraim; the trees themselves would fight for David that day."},
{q:"How many of Absalom's men fell that day?", options:["Twenty thousand","Ten thousand","Three thousand","Forty thousand"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 18:7",verse:"Where the people of Israel were slain before the servants of David, and there was there a great slaughter that day of twenty thousand men.", insight:"Twenty thousand fell; rebellion is expensive, and the bill always comes due."},
{q:"What devoured more people than the sword that day?", options:["The wood","The river Jordan","A sudden plague","Wild beasts"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 18:8",verse:"For the battle was there scattered over the face of all the country: and the wood devoured more people that day than the sword devoured.", insight:"The wood devoured more than the sword; creation itself turned against the rebellion."},
{q:"How was Absalom caught in the oak?", options:["His head caught hold of the oak, and the mule went away from under him","His armor snagged on a branch","His spear stuck in the trunk","His cloak tangled in the boughs"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 18:9",verse:"And Absalom met the servants of David. And Absalom rode upon a mule, and the mule went under the thick boughs of a great oak, and his head caught hold of the oak, and he was taken up between the heaven and the earth; and the mule that was under him went away.", insight:"Hung between heaven and earth; the proud prince dangled where everyone could see."},
{q:"Who reported Absalom's plight to Joab?", options:["A certain man who saw it","Ahimaaz the son of Zadok","One of the ten armor bearers","A watchman from the wall"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 18:10",verse:"And a certain man saw it, and told Joab, and said, Behold, I saw Absalom hanged in an oak.", insight:"A certain man, unnamed; God often works through witnesses history forgets."},
{q:"What reward did Joab offer the man for killing Absalom?", options:["Ten shekels of silver, and a girdle","A hundred shekels and a horse","A captain's place in the host","The king's own sword"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 18:11",verse:"And Joab said unto the man that told him, And, behold, thou sawest him, and why didst thou not smite him there to the ground? and I would have given thee ten shekels of silver, and a girdle.", insight:"Ten shekels and a girdle; Joab priced disobedience cheap and the man would not buy."},
{q:"Why did the man refuse to touch the king's son?", options:["In our hearing the king charged, Beware that none touch the young man Absalom","He feared Absalom's guards","He had sworn an oath to Absalom","He wanted a greater reward"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 18:12",verse:"And the man said unto Joab, Though I should receive a thousand shekels of silver in mine hand, yet would I not put forth mine hand against the king’s son: for in our hearing the king charged thee and Abishai and Ittai, saying, Beware that none touch the young man Absalom.", insight:"He remembered the king's charge when Joab forgot it; a common soldier kept the word the captain broke."},
{q:"What did Joab thrust through Absalom's heart?", options:["Three darts, while he was yet alive in the midst of the oak","A spear from his chariot","His sword, twice","A javelin from afar"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 18:14",verse:"Then said Joab, I may not tarry thus with thee. And he took three darts in his hand, and thrust them through the heart of Absalom, while he was yet alive in the midst of the oak.", insight:"Three darts through the heart; Joab's loyalty to David stopped short of David's mercy."},
{q:"Who finished the killing of Absalom?", options:["Ten young men that bare Joab's armour","Abishai with his spear","The certain man who found him","David's own guard"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 18:15",verse:"And ten young men that bare Joab’s armour compassed about and smote Absalom, and slew him.", insight:"Ten armor bearers finished it; many hands share the guilt of one disobedience."},
{q:"How did Joab stop the slaughter?", options:["He blew the trumpet, and the people returned","He raised a white banner","He sent runners through the wood","He called on the name of the LORD"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 18:16",verse:"And Joab blew the trumpet, and the people returned from pursuing after Israel: for Joab held back the people.", insight:"The trumpet blew; even Joab knew when enough blood had been shed."},
{q:"What did they do with Absalom's body?", options:["Cast him into a great pit in the wood, and laid a great heap of stones upon him","Buried him in the king's sepulchre","Burned him with fire","Left him hanging in the oak"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 18:17",verse:"And they took Absalom, and cast him into a great pit in the wood, and laid a very great heap of stones upon him: and all Israel fled every one to his tent.", insight:"A pit and a heap of stones; the monument of a rebel is a warning, not a tomb."},
{q:"What had Absalom set up in his lifetime in the king's dale?", options:["A pillar, because he had no son to keep his name in remembrance","A tower of carved stone","An altar to the LORD","A statue of himself in gold"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 18:18",verse:"Now Absalom in his lifetime had taken and reared up for himself a pillar, which is in the king’s dale: for he said, I have no son to keep my name in remembrance: and he called the pillar after his own name: and it is called unto this day, Absalom’s place.", insight:"A pillar for his name, since he had no son; he built a memorial because he feared being forgotten."},
{q:"Who first asked to run and bear the tidings to David?", options:["Ahimaaz the son of Zadok","Cushi the messenger","Jonathan the son of Abiathar","Joab himself"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 18:19",verse:"Then said Ahimaaz the son of Zadok, Let me now run, and bear the king tidings, how that the LORD hath avenged him of his enemies.", insight:"Ahimaaz was eager to run; zeal to bring news is not the same as wisdom to bear it."},
{q:"Why did Joab refuse to let Ahimaaz go?", options:["Because the king's son is dead","Because the road was not safe","Because Cushi was the faster runner","Because David had forbidden runners"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 18:20",verse:"And Joab said unto him, Thou shalt not bear tidings this day, but thou shalt bear tidings another day: but this day thou shalt bear no tidings, because the king’s son is dead.", insight:"'Thou hast no tidings ready'; Joab knew this news would break the king."},
{q:"Whom did Joab send with the tidings instead?", options:["Cushi","Abiathar","Zadok","Hushai"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 18:21",verse:"Then said Joab to Cushi, Go tell the king what thou hast seen. And Cushi bowed himself unto Joab, and ran.", insight:"Cushi bore the hard message; some errands fall to those with no ties to soften them."},
{q:"What question did David ask of the runners?", options:["Is the young man Absalom safe?","Who won the battle?","Where is Joab?","How many fell?"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 18:29",verse:"And the king said, Is the young man Absalom safe? And Ahimaaz answered, When Joab sent the king’s servant, and me thy servant, I saw a great tumult, but I knew not what it was.", insight:"Not 'did we win' but 'is Absalom safe'; the father's first question was for his son."},
{q:"What was David's cry when he heard?", options:["O my son Absalom, my son, my son Absalom! would God I had died for thee","The LORD has judged righteously","Bury him with honor","Let the trumpets sound"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 18:33",verse:"And the king was much moved, and went up to the chamber over the gate, and wept: and as he went, thus he said, O my son Absalom, my son, my son Absalom! would God I had died for thee, O Absalom, my son, my son!", insight:"'Would God I had died for thee'; grief poured out where justice had already been done."}
]},
{n:19, name:"The King's Return", seal:{ref:"2 Samuel 19:30",verse:"And Mephibosheth said unto the king, Yea, let him take all, forasmuch as my lord the king is come again in peace unto his own house."}, facts:["Did you know Joab told David to his face that he loved his enemies and hated his friends, and swore that not one servant would stay with him that night if he did not greet them (2 Samuel 19:6-7)?","Did you know Mephibosheth had neither dressed his feet, nor trimmed his beard, nor washed his clothes from the day David fled Jerusalem until his return (2 Samuel 19:24)?","Did you know Barzillai was eighty years old when he declined David's invitation to Jerusalem, saying he could no longer taste food or hear singing, and sent his servant Chimham in his place (2 Samuel 19:32, 19:35, 19:37)?"], questions:[
{q:"What was told to Joab?", options:["Behold, the king weepeth and mourneth for Absalom","The king has fled to Mahanaim","Absalom lives and hides in Ephraim","The people demand a new king"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 19:1",verse:"And it was told Joab, Behold, the king weepeth and mourneth for Absalom.", insight:"The king wept for the rebel; victory felt like defeat in David's tent."},
{q:"What did the victory turn into that day?", options:["Mourning unto all the people","A great feast in Jerusalem","A new covenant with Israel","A song of triumph"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 19:2",verse:"And the victory that day was turned into mourning unto all the people: for the people heard say that day how the king was grieved for his son.", insight:"Victory turned to mourning; when the leader grieves, the whole camp feels it."},
{q:"How did the people steal into the city that day?", options:["By stealth, as people ashamed steal away when they flee in battle","With trumpets and shouting","In battle array with banners","Through the water gate at night"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 19:3",verse:"And the people gat them by stealth that day into the city, as people being ashamed steal away when they flee in battle.", insight:"They crept in like defeated men; their king's tears had stolen their triumph."},
{q:"What did David cry with a loud voice?", options:["O my son Absalom, O Absalom, my son, my son!","O LORD, why hast Thou forsaken me","O Joab, what hast thou done","O Jerusalem, my city"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 19:4",verse:"But the king covered his face, and the king cried with a loud voice, O my son Absalom, O Absalom, my son, my son!", insight:"He covered his face and cried aloud; great kings grieve out loud too."},
{q:"What did Joab say David had done to his servants?", options:["Shamed the faces of all who had saved his life that day","Robbed them of their spoil","Sent them into exile","Forgotten their names"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 19:5",verse:"And Joab came into the house to the king, and said, Thou hast shamed this day the faces of all thy servants, which this day have saved thy life, and the lives of thy sons and of thy daughters, and the lives of thy wives, and the lives of thy concubines;", insight:"'Thou hast shamed this day the faces of all thy servants'; Joab spoke hard truth to a grieving king."},
{q:"What hard charge did Joab lay on David?", options:["Thou lovest thine enemies, and hatest thy friends","Thou hast broken the covenant","Thou fearest thy own people","Thou trustest in chariots"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 19:6",verse:"In that thou lovest thine enemies, and hatest thy friends. For thou hast declared this day, that thou regardest neither princes nor servants: for this day I perceive, that if Absalom had lived, and all we had died this day, then it had pleased thee well.", insight:"'Thou lovest thine enemies, and hatest thy friends'; grief had flipped David's loves upside down."},
{q:"What did Joab swear would happen if David did not go forth?", options:["There will not tarry one with thee this night","Absalom's men would return","The Philistines would invade","The ark would be taken"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 19:7",verse:"Now therefore arise, go forth, and speak comfortably unto thy servants: for I swear by the LORD, if thou go not forth, there will not tarry one with thee this night: and that will be worse unto thee than all the evil that befell thee from thy youth until now.", insight:"Not one would tarry; Joab used fear to move a king frozen by sorrow."},
{q:"What did David do then?", options:["He arose, and sat in the gate","He fled to his chamber","He called for the priests","He wrote a psalm of lament"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 19:8",verse:"Then the king arose, and sat in the gate. And they told unto all the people, saying, Behold, the king doth sit in the gate. And all the people came before the king: for Israel had fled every man to his tent.", insight:"He sat in the gate; showing up is sometimes the whole duty of a king."},
{q:"What were the tribes saying throughout Israel?", options:["The king saved us from our enemies, and now he is fled for Absalom","Let us make Joab king","We will serve Absalom's son","David is too old to reign"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 19:9",verse:"And all the people were at strife throughout all the tribes of Israel, saying, The king saved us out of the hand of our enemies, and he delivered us out of the hand of the Philistines; and now he is fled out of the land for Absalom.", insight:"They remembered his deliverances; gratitude was stirring them back to loyalty."},
{q:"What question did Israel ask about bringing the king back?", options:["Why speak ye not a word of bringing the king back?","Who will pay for the war?","Shall Joab be punished?","Where is the ark of God?"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 19:10",verse:"And Absalom, whom we anointed over us, is dead in battle. Now therefore why speak ye not a word of bringing the king back?", insight:"'Why speak ye not a word?'; sometimes loyalty only needs someone to say it first."},
{q:"What did David ask the elders of Judah through the priests?", options:["Why are ye the last to bring the king back to his house?","Will ye anoint my son Solomon?","Where are the men of Benjamin?","Who will go with me to Gilgal?"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 19:11",verse:"And king David sent to Zadok and to Abiathar the priests, saying, Speak unto the elders of Judah, saying, Why are ye the last to bring the king back to his house? seeing the speech of all Israel is come to the king, even to his house.", insight:"'Why are ye the last?'; David shamed his own tribe into leading the return."},
{q:"What did David promise Amasa?", options:["Thou shalt be captain of the host before me continually in the room of Joab","Thou shalt rule over Judah","Thou shalt have Absalom's lands","Thou shalt be priest instead of Abiathar"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 19:13",verse:"And say ye to Amasa, Art thou not of my bone, and of my flesh? God do so to me, and more also, if thou be not captain of the host before me continually in the room of Joab.", insight:"Amasa, Absalom's captain, was offered Joab's place; David reached for his enemies to heal the nation."},
{q:"What effect did David's words have on Judah?", options:["He bowed the heart of all the men of Judah, even as the heart of one man","They demanded Joab's death","Half of them refused to come","They asked for three days to decide"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 19:14",verse:"And he bowed the heart of all the men of Judah, even as the heart of one man; so that they sent this word unto the king, Return thou, and all thy servants.", insight:"One heart in all Judah; the right words can knit a divided people."},
{q:"Who fell down before David at the Jordan?", options:["Shimei the son of Gera","Ziba the servant","Amasa the captain","Barzillai the Gileadite"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 19:18",verse:"And there went over a ferry boat to carry over the king’s household, and to do what he thought good. And Shimei the son of Gera fell down before the king, as he was come over Jordan;", insight:"Shimei fell down where he had once thrown stones; the curser came crawling back."},
{q:"What did Shimei confess to David?", options:["Thy servant doth know that I have sinned","I was forced by Absalom","Abishai made me curse","I never threw the stones"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 19:20",verse:"For thy servant doth know that I have sinned: therefore, behold, I am come the first this day of all the house of Joseph to go down to meet my lord the king.", insight:"'I have sinned'; Shimei's confession was quick, and perhaps too convenient."},
{q:"What did Abishai say about Shimei?", options:["Shall not Shimei be put to death, because he cursed the LORD's anointed?","Let Shimei be made a servant","Shimei should be exiled to Moab","Shimei's house should be burned"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 19:21",verse:"But Abishai the son of Zeruiah answered and said, Shall not Shimei be put to death for this, because he cursed the LORD’S anointed?", insight:"Abishai remembered the stones; justice has a long memory, but mercy must be longer."},
{q:"What did David swear to Shimei?", options:["Thou shalt not die","Thou shalt serve me all thy days","Thy sons shall be princes","Thou shalt leave Israel"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 19:23",verse:"Therefore the king said unto Shimei, Thou shalt not die. And the king sware unto him.", insight:"'Thou shalt not die'; on restoration day David chose mercy over revenge."},
{q:"What had Mephibosheth neglected since David left Jerusalem?", options:["He had neither dressed his feet, nor trimmed his beard, nor washed his clothes","He had not eaten bread nor drunk wine","He had not left his house at all","He had not spoken a single word"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 19:24",verse:"And Mephibosheth the son of Saul came down to meet the king, and had neither dressed his feet, nor trimmed his beard, nor washed his clothes, from the day the king departed until the day he came again in peace.", insight:"Unwashed, untrimmed, undressed feet; his body had been mourning what his mouth could not say."},
{q:"How did Mephibosheth explain staying behind?", options:["My servant deceived me, for thy servant said, I will saddle me an ass","He was sick with a fever","Absalom's men held him prisoner","He feared David would not return"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 19:26",verse:"And he answered, My lord, O king, my servant deceived me: for thy servant said, I will saddle me an ass, that I may ride thereon, and go to the king; because thy servant is lame.", insight:"'My servant deceived me'; Ziba's slander had kept the lame man home."},
{q:"What did Mephibosheth say when David divided the land with Ziba?", options:["Yea, let him take all, forasmuch as my lord the king is come again in peace","Divide it fairly, my lord","Give it all to Ziba, he deserves it","I will appeal to the priests"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 19:30",verse:"And Mephibosheth said unto the king, Yea, let him take all, forasmuch as my lord the king is come again in peace unto his own house.", insight:"'Let him take all'; Mephibosheth wanted the king, not the land."}
]},
{n:20, name:"Sheba's Rebellion", seal:{ref:"2 Samuel 20:19",verse:"I am one of them that are peaceable and faithful in Israel: thou seekest to destroy a city and a mother in Israel: why wilt thou swallow up the inheritance of the LORD?"}, facts:["Did you know David shut the ten concubines Absalom had defiled in ward for life, feeding them but never visiting them, and they lived in widowhood until they died (2 Samuel 20:3)?","Did you know the wise woman of Abel saved her city by reminding Joab that in old time people said, 'They shall surely ask counsel at Abel' (2 Samuel 20:18)?","Did you know Sheba's rebellion ended with his head thrown over the wall to Joab, and David's restored government closed with Ira the Jairite as a chief ruler about David (2 Samuel 20:22, 20:26)?"], questions:[
{q:"Who blew the trumpet of rebellion after Absalom's fall?", options:["Sheba the son of Bichri, a Benjamite","Shimei the son of Gera","Amasa the son of Ithra","Adonijah the son of Haggith"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 20:1",verse:"And there happened to be there a man of Belial, whose name was Sheba, the son of Bichri, a Benjamite: and he blew a trumpet, and said, We have no part in David, neither have we inheritance in the son of Jesse: every man to his tents, O Israel.", insight:"Sheba, a man of Belial; every restored kingdom gets tested by a new rebel."},
{q:"What was Sheba's cry?", options:["We have no part in David, neither have we inheritance in the son of Jesse: every man to his tents, O Israel","Down with the house of David forever","Make Sheba king in Hebron","To your tents, O Judah"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 20:1",verse:"And there happened to be there a man of Belial, whose name was Sheba, the son of Bichri, a Benjamite: and he blew a trumpet, and said, We have no part in David, neither have we inheritance in the son of Jesse: every man to his tents, O Israel.", insight:"'No part in David'; the same old cry, from the same old spirit of division."},
{q:"Who followed Sheba?", options:["Every man of Israel","Only the Benjamites","The men of Judah","The Philistines"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 20:2",verse:"So every man of Israel went up from after David, and followed Sheba the son of Bichri: but the men of Judah clave unto their king, from Jordan even to Jerusalem.", insight:"Every man of Israel went up from David; the quarrel at Jordan bore bitter fruit."},
{q:"Who stayed loyal to David?", options:["The men of Judah, from Jordan even to Jerusalem","The Benjamites","The Gileadites only","None at all"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 20:2",verse:"So every man of Israel went up from after David, and followed Sheba the son of Bichri: but the men of Judah clave unto their king, from Jordan even to Jerusalem.", insight:"Judah clave unto their king; loyalty held where kinship ran deepest."},
{q:"What became of the ten concubines Absalom had defiled?", options:["David put them in ward, fed them, and they lived in widowhood till death","They were sent back to their fathers","They were given to Amasa's men","They fled to the Philistines"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 20:3",verse:"And David came to his house at Jerusalem; and the king took the ten women his concubines, whom he had left to keep the house, and put them in ward, and fed them, but went not in unto them. So they were shut up unto the day of their death, living in widowhood.", insight:"Shut up in widowhood, fed but never visited; Absalom's sin left them in a living grief."},
{q:"What did David command Amasa to do?", options:["Assemble the men of Judah within three days","Pursue Sheba at once alone","Bring the ark to Jerusalem","Number the fighting men"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 20:4",verse:"Then said the king to Amasa, Assemble me the men of Judah within three days, and be thou here present.", insight:"Three days to muster Judah; David gave his new captain his first test."},
{q:"What went wrong with Amasa's muster?", options:["He tarried longer than the set time","He joined Sheba's rebellion","He lost half the men","He refused the command"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 20:5",verse:"So Amasa went to assemble the men of Judah: but he tarried longer than the set time which he had appointed him.", insight:"He tarried longer than the set time; delay in duty can be deadly."},
{q:"What did David say about Sheba to Abishai?", options:["Now shall Sheba do us more harm than did Absalom","Sheba is nothing but a fool","Let Sheba go in peace","Sheba will surrender by morning"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 20:6",verse:"And David said to Abishai, Now shall Sheba the son of Bichri do us more harm than did Absalom: take thou thy lord’s servants, and pursue after him, lest he get him fenced cities, and escape us.", insight:"'More harm than did Absalom'; David knew small rebellions grow when ignored."},
{q:"Who went out to pursue Sheba?", options:["Joab's men, and the Cherethites, and the Pelethites, and all the mighty men","Amasa and the men of Judah alone","Abishai with the Benjamites","David himself with his guard"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 20:7",verse:"And there went out after him Joab’s men, and the Cherethites, and the Pelethites, and all the mighty men: and they went out of Jerusalem, to pursue after Sheba the son of Bichri.", insight:"Joab's men went too, uninvited; Joab never stayed out of a fight for long."},
{q:"Where did Joab meet Amasa?", options:["At the great stone which is in Gibeon","At the well of Bahurim","By the ford of Jordan","At the gate of Mahanaim"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 20:8",verse:"When they were at the great stone which is in Gibeon, Amasa went before them. And Joab’s garment that he had put on was girded unto him, and upon it a girdle with a sword fastened upon his loins in the sheath thereof; and as he went forth it fell out.", insight:"At the great stone in Gibeon; landmarks remember what men do beside them."},
{q:"What greeting did Joab give Amasa?", options:["Art thou in health, my brother?","Hail, captain of Judah","Peace be to thee","The king sends for thee"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 20:9",verse:"And Joab said to Amasa, Art thou in health, my brother? And Joab took Amasa by the beard with the right hand to kiss him.", insight:"'Art thou in health, my brother?'; murder wore a brother's greeting."},
{q:"How did Joab take hold of Amasa?", options:["By the beard with his right hand, to kiss him","By the hand in friendship","By the shoulder to embrace him","By the arm to steady him"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 20:9",verse:"And Joab said to Amasa, Art thou in health, my brother? And Joab took Amasa by the beard with the right hand to kiss him.", insight:"A kiss for a cover; the oldest treachery wears the warmest face."},
{q:"Where did Joab's sword strike Amasa?", options:["In the fifth rib, and shed out his bowels to the ground","In the throat","Between the shoulders","Through the heart"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 20:10",verse:"But Amasa took no heed to the sword that was in Joab’s hand: so he smote him therewith in the fifth rib, and shed out his bowels to the ground, and struck him not again; and he died. So Joab and Abishai his brother pursued after Sheba the son of Bichri.", insight:"One stroke in the fifth rib; Amasa never saw the sword in the kiss."},
{q:"What did Joab's man cry to the troops?", options:["He that favoureth Joab, and he that is for David, let him go after Joab","Avenge Amasa, our captain","Stone the murderer","Return to Jerusalem"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 20:11",verse:"And one of Joab’s men stood by him, and said, He that favoureth Joab, and he that is for David, let him go after Joab.", insight:"'He that is for David, let him go after Joab'; Joab claimed David's name for his own bloody work."},
{q:"What did they do with Amasa's body?", options:["They removed him into the field and cast a cloth upon him","They buried him at Gibeon","They left him in the highway","They carried him to David"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 20:12",verse:"And Amasa wallowed in blood in the midst of the highway. And when the man saw that all the people stood still, he removed Amasa out of the highway into the field, and cast a cloth upon him, when he saw that every one that came by him stood still.", insight:"A cloth over the body in the field; they hid the murder so the march could go on."},
{q:"Where was Sheba besieged?", options:["In Abel of Bethmaachah","In Jerusalem","In Gibeon","In Mahanaim"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 20:15",verse:"And they came and besieged him in Abel of Beth-maachah, and they cast up a bank against the city, and it stood in the trench: and all the people that were with Joab battered the wall, to throw it down.", insight:"Abel of Bethmaachah; the rebel ran to a city famous for wisdom."},
{q:"Who called out to Joab from the wall?", options:["A wise woman out of the city","The elders of Abel","Sheba himself","A priest of the city"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 20:16",verse:"Then cried a wise woman out of the city, Hear, hear; say, I pray you, unto Joab, Come near hither, that I may speak with thee.", insight:"A wise woman cried, 'Hear, hear'; wisdom spoke up while the battering rams worked."},
{q:"What did the woman say about Abel in old time?", options:["They shall surely ask counsel at Abel","It never opened its gates","Its walls had never fallen","Kings were crowned there"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 20:18",verse:"Then she spake, saying, They were wont to speak in old time, saying, They shall surely ask counsel at Abel: and so they ended the matter.", insight:"'They shall surely ask counsel at Abel'; she reminded Joab what the city was before he destroyed it."},
{q:"What did Joab demand of the city?", options:["Deliver Sheba only, and I will depart from the city","Open the gates to my army","Pay tribute of silver and gold","Surrender all who followed Sheba"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 20:21",verse:"The matter is not so: but a man of mount Ephraim, Sheba the son of Bichri by name, hath lifted up his hand against the king, even against David: deliver him only, and I will depart from the city. And the woman said unto Joab, Behold, his head shall be thrown to thee over the wall.", insight:"'Deliver him only'; Joab wanted one head, not a ruined city."},
{q:"How did Sheba's rebellion end?", options:["They cut off Sheba's head and cast it out to Joab over the wall","Sheba escaped to the Philistines","The city surrendered and paid tribute","Joab battered down the wall"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 20:22",verse:"Then the woman went unto all the people in her wisdom. And they cut off the head of Sheba the son of Bichri, and cast it out to Joab. And he blew a trumpet, and they retired from the city, every man to his tent. And Joab returned to Jerusalem unto the king.", insight:"A head over the wall, and the trumpet blew; wisdom ended what weapons had started."}
]}
]);
